sieve-filter-v2
; No leap between neighbouring notes wider than `leap` semitones: melodies that move mostly by
; small steps sound calm and singable, big jumps restless. Rests are passed over (the next note is
; measured from the last note before them), or, with rest_resets, a rest lets the next note be
; anything. The state is the last note's pitch (0: none yet).
id        melody-leap
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes*
describe  No two neighbouring notes further apart than the leap, in semitones.
param     leap         int     4  1  24  the widest step between neighbouring notes, in semitones
param     rest_resets  choice  no no,yes whether a rest lets the next note be anything

states    {PITCHES + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{PITCHES}
for d 0 {DURATIONS - 1}
  t 0 @{d} 0
  for p 1 {PITCHES}
    t 0 @{p * DURATIONS + d} {p}
    if {rest_resets == 1}
      t {p} @{d} 0
    else
      t {p} @{d} {p}
    fi
    for q {max(1, p - leap)} {min(PITCHES, p + leap)}
      t {p} @{q * DURATIONS + d} {q}
    done
  done
done
end
